IMPLEMENTATION LIMITS (NOT POSIX / NOT CPYTHON)

Execution and RAM
  6 user-process slots; each slot 24 KiB including 4 KiB stack.
  MCP execute_command itself uses sh and a child program.
  File descriptors are limited (typically 16 per process).
  RAM FS files are small: max 2048 bytes; check free space.

MCP shell mode
  execute_command <=119 ASCII bytes; output capped at 4096 B;
  typical command timeout 3000 ms; PTY tools available for interactive programs (one session).
  write_file: /tmp/NAME ASCII only, <=2048 B, overwrites file.
  get_manual: individual ROM pages via topic; not all pages at once.

C compiler cc
  source 1024 B; generated assembly buffer 4096 B;
  up to 16 functions; up to 4 parameters per function;
  up to 16 variables per function; local frame <=256 B;
  up to 64 elements per local array; no full C stdlib/preprocessor.
  A large generated .s may exceed as input capacity.

Assembler as
  source <=2048 B; output code <=2040 B + 8-byte PNX1 header;
  up to 32 local labels; only implemented subset of Thumb-1.
  Destination is /tmp/a.out.

Python-like interpreter
  script <=2048 B; <=64 nonempty lines; no tabs for indentation;
  <=16 variables; identifiers stored in max 15 characters;
  string <=64 bytes; list/bytes <=64 elements;
  shared value pool 256 32-bit words; block nesting <=8;
  while/for iterations each <=10000; msleep <=60000 ms.

These constraints are from current source, not a stable API contract.
Read /man/languages/c, /man/languages/asm, /man/languages/python
before generating code. If tool reports failure, inspect first.

IMPORTANT: 56 KiB kernel is RESERVED SRAM REGION, not measured used
bytes. Six process slots and eleven RAM-file entries are separate.
RAM files max 2048 bytes each; cc may generate .s >2048 bytes even
from a C source <=1024 bytes. See process-resources and c-debug.
